00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:36.190
Will I ever again rejoice in the forest like before?

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:42.870
Mattis and Borka's conflict had flared up, leaving Ronja isolated in her sadness.

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:52.920
Then one day, Ronja came home to find Birk captured and in bad shape.

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:56.110
Crying out "I hate you!",

00:01:56.110 --> 00:02:01.890
Ronja suddenly detested her previously-beloved father.

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:06.430
Mattis!

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:12.690
The Endless Dispute (Part 2)

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:12.690
The Endless Dispute (Part 2)

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:28.800
They're here.

00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:43.260
Birk!

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:26.280
Birk! Birk! Are you okay?!

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:30.280
Mattis! You bastard!

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:31.900
You dirty beast!

00:04:31.900 --> 00:04:35.330
Give me my Birk back already!

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:39.250
Otherwise, I'll gouge out your eyes!

00:04:39.990 --> 00:04:42.690
Do you hear me, you hoodlums?!

00:04:42.690 --> 00:04:45.340
Why don't you say something?

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:50.390
Or have your actions left your tongue-tied with shame?

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:54.010
What are you thinking, eh? Mattis!

00:04:54.010 --> 00:04:57.520
Can you shut your woman up, Borka?

00:04:57.520 --> 00:05:03.400
It would be best for you to hear what I have to say.

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:05.500
What?!

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:08.360
Why have you kept quiet all this while?

00:05:08.360 --> 00:05:11.040
Why don't you say something!

00:05:13.050 --> 00:05:16.640
You're a hard man, Mattis.

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:19.880
Stop it, you guys! Let me go!

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:22.380
And a vile person.

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:27.130
I can understand that you want me out of here...

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:29.800
But, Mattis...

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:35.960
Using my child to get your way is reprehensible.

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:39.980
I couldn't care less what you think.

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:44.820
What I <i>do</i> want to know is how soon you're going to leave.

00:05:59.410 --> 00:06:04.780
First, I have to find a place where we can settle down safely.

00:06:04.780 --> 00:06:07.670
That may be difficult.

00:06:07.670 --> 00:06:12.640
But if you give me back my son,

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:17.680
you have my word that we will be gone before the summer is over.

00:06:18.370 --> 00:06:19.640
Fair enough.

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:27.440
Then you have my word that you will get your son back before the summer's end.

00:06:28.580 --> 00:06:35.330
I meant that I want him back this instant.

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:39.040
And I meant that you won't be getting him.

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:42.170
Bastard!

00:06:42.170 --> 00:06:45.500
May the wild harpies carry you off!

00:06:48.790 --> 00:06:53.970
However, Borka, we have dungeons in Mattis' Fort.

00:06:53.970 --> 00:06:57.370
He will not want for a roof over his head.

00:06:57.370 --> 00:07:06.840
So let that be a comfort to you if it happens to be a rainy summer.

00:07:28.930 --> 00:07:31.900
Those dungeons should be utterly demolished!

00:07:32.890 --> 00:07:36.720
You deserve to be in trouble too, Father!

00:08:08.690 --> 00:08:12.920
<i>What's the matter with you? Don't you feel well?</i>

00:08:22.590 --> 00:08:27.040
<i>Why didn't you jump? Now, I'm coming!</i>

00:08:30.460 --> 00:08:32.820
<i>Follow that, if you can!</i>

00:09:55.650 --> 00:09:59.240
We have dungeons underground on this side too.

00:10:00.120 --> 00:10:04.740
Your daughter will not want for a roof over her head either.

00:10:05.610 --> 00:10:07.750
You should take comfort in that!

00:10:08.140 --> 00:10:09.500
Mattis!

00:10:14.420 --> 00:10:21.430
You <i>should</i> cry. I'd would too, if I had a monster like that for a father.

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:23.850
Mind your own business.

00:10:25.470 --> 00:10:28.480
Nobody asked you to stick your nose in here.

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:29.890
What?

00:10:52.750 --> 00:10:55.140
Well, Mattis!

00:10:55.140 --> 00:11:00.470
Are you going to give me back my son, or not?!

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:13.270
You! Are you going to give me back my son, or not?!

00:11:14.140 --> 00:11:16.420
Of course I will.

00:11:17.170 --> 00:11:19.560
Whenever you want.

00:11:20.150 --> 00:11:22.040
I want him now!

00:11:22.040 --> 00:11:26.910
Not when summer is over. Right this instant!

00:11:28.980 --> 00:11:30.620
As you wish.

00:11:33.410 --> 00:11:38.260
I'm not a vengeful or petty man.

00:11:38.260 --> 00:11:40.970
Fair exchange is no robbery.

00:11:41.900 --> 00:11:46.780
If you return my son, I'll give your daughter back too.

00:11:46.780 --> 00:11:48.470
You scoundrel!

00:11:50.880 --> 00:11:53.380
I have no child.

00:11:59.310 --> 00:12:02.040
I have no child.

00:12:06.780 --> 00:12:09.330
What do you mean by that?

00:12:09.330 --> 00:12:15.040
Is this some new mischief you're plotting?

00:12:20.100 --> 00:12:23.450
Come and get your son, Borka.

00:12:23.450 --> 00:12:28.340
But you can't give me back my child,

00:12:29.960 --> 00:12:33.470
for I have none, after all.

00:12:33.470 --> 00:12:37.400
But, I have a child!

00:12:40.900 --> 00:12:43.780
And I want my daughter back!

00:12:43.780 --> 00:12:45.260
Immediately!

00:12:45.260 --> 00:12:47.910
Understand, Borka?!

00:12:48.900 --> 00:12:54.480
Even if her father's acting like a total fool.

00:13:21.440 --> 00:13:26.440
Ronja, the Robber's Daughter

00:13:21.440 --> 00:13:26.440
Ronja, the Robber's Daughter

00:13:41.450 --> 00:13:42.580
Let's go.

00:14:01.300 --> 00:14:02.340
They're coming!

00:14:30.490 --> 00:14:32.800
Where's Mattis?

00:14:32.800 --> 00:14:35.000
Who knows?! Dammit!

00:14:36.220 --> 00:14:40.580
He might not feel like up to facing Ronja.

00:15:47.700 --> 00:15:52.520
I'm impressed a kidnapper like Mattis can even feel shame at all!

00:15:52.520 --> 00:15:56.180
I can understand why he's too embarrassed to show his face.

00:16:18.820 --> 00:16:19.800
Now.

00:16:48.520 --> 00:16:50.430
What are you doing?

00:16:51.390 --> 00:16:53.230
She's my sister.

00:16:53.550 --> 00:16:56.670
She saved my life.

00:16:57.690 --> 00:17:01.240
She saved... your life?

00:17:05.840 --> 00:17:10.750
Just as Birk saved mine.

00:17:12.150 --> 00:17:18.930
Has my son been keeping company with my enemy's offspring behind my back?

00:17:22.040 --> 00:17:25.300
She's my sister, like I said.

00:17:32.770 --> 00:17:34.840
Sister?!

00:17:34.840 --> 00:17:36.750
Yeah, <i>sure</i> !

00:17:36.750 --> 00:17:42.960
We all know what that will mean in a couple more years!

00:17:42.960 --> 00:17:44.360
Now, we're leaving!

00:17:47.350 --> 00:17:49.290
Don't touch me!

00:17:51.540 --> 00:17:53.340
I'll go by myself!

00:17:53.780 --> 00:17:57.550
And you can keep your hands off of me!

00:18:02.050 --> 00:18:03.450
Birk!

00:18:05.240 --> 00:18:07.060
Birk!

00:18:38.380 --> 00:18:42.430
Ronja. Were you with Borka's son...

00:18:46.220 --> 00:18:49.090
Don't talk to me.

00:19:12.710 --> 00:19:14.600
Oh, it's Ronja!

00:19:14.600 --> 00:19:16.960
Ronja!

00:19:16.960 --> 00:19:18.490
Cut it out!

00:19:18.920 --> 00:19:20.260
Why?

00:19:20.850 --> 00:19:23.380
Ronja!

00:19:23.790 --> 00:19:25.660
Welcome back!

00:19:25.660 --> 00:19:27.430
Ronja!

00:19:27.940 --> 00:19:29.130
Ronja?

00:20:18.020 --> 00:20:23.620
Oh, Ronja! I'm so glad you're back alive!

00:20:24.600 --> 00:20:26.450
Poor child.

00:20:26.450 --> 00:20:30.500
I've been so worried about you.

00:20:38.460 --> 00:20:42.810
There's nothing but misery in Mattis' fort lately.

00:20:57.780 --> 00:21:01.400
I've got Mattis in my bedroom,

00:21:03.770 --> 00:21:12.040
but he just lies there, staring, and never says a word.

00:21:14.780 --> 00:21:18.510
He won't get up, and he doesn't want to eat.

00:21:23.640 --> 00:21:26.850
What will we do with him?

00:21:29.620 --> 00:21:33.190
He'll come when he's hungry enough.

